            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Conley and Taber (2011) and Ferman and Pinto (2019) study inference with few treated groups. Their procedures use the cross-sectional distribution of estimated shocks among many control groups to approximate the distribution of the treated groups' shocks. The present approach instead uses the time-series distribution of pre-treatment differential trends for the same treated and control groups.",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                1313,
                1086,
                1448
